class_name SideTrialPlans
extends RefCounted
## Floor plans of the jump trial (Sprungprobe, SV2, D-195): four per biome on top of the six of
## SidePlans (rounds 1-3), each also mirrored, with a tier (1-3). Same legend as SidePlans plus the
## elements of dungeon/side/elements/ and the side enemies of SV4:
##   M  moving platform (sideways along -)     V  moving platform (up and down along |)
##   j  spring (4.5 tiles)                     // tilting platform (falls 0.4 s after a touch)
##   _  collapsing bridge piece                X  saw on its rail of +
##   *  wall-jump shaft (air between rock walls)
##   L  lantern (safe return spot)             b  bat   i  spike hedgehog   u  shield bearer
## Tier 1 plans bring one new element alone (each element appears alone in tier 1 first), tier 2
## two, tier 3 three and more with narrow steps and timed parts; tall plans (up to 22 rows) and
## plans from tier 2 have a lantern before the hard part. Rules: SideLayout.check (also
## tests/unit/test_side_layout.gd); the bot makes every one: dungeon/side/side_check.gd pieces=1.
## D-216: each is the hard part of one obstacle run (ObstacleRunPlans); the dash gaps became gaps
## of three tiles for the double jump (no side dash).
## Generated from a painted canvas (rooms-dev scratch script); edit the rows directly, then run
## the side check.

